{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Surely I have seen the affliction of my people.</b> The righteous of the generation — who sigh and groan over the transgressions of the generation and over the poor, and pray — it was corresponding to them that the angel of YHWH appeared within the bush. The sense of רָאֹה רָאִיתִי is: I have indeed seen. This is the force of the root whenever it is doubled, as in עָלֹה נַעֲלֶה, יָכֹל נוּכַל (Numbers 13:30), for its meaning is like 'indeed,' to indicate that the truth is so even though a disputant may claim the opposite, as in יָדַעְתִּי בְנִי יָדַעְתִּי (Genesis 48:19) — that is: even though I have seen the affliction of my people who are in Egypt, as the presence of the angel in the bush made known, and though I will turn my hand against their foes, as the fire in the bush made known, nevertheless the Egyptians who oppress them will not be consumed by all the plagues I send upon them, as וְהַסְּנֶה אֵינֶנּוּ אֻכָּל made known. For the plagues I bring upon them are not intended to destroy them and settle Israel in their place, but to deliver Israel from their hand and bring them to another place."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:10.124262315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}